---

# Running the Project

The project requires 4 terminals.

Project directory:

cd D:\Lifeguard_ai\backend

---

## Terminal 1 — MQTT Broker

Run:

& "C:\Program Files\mosquitto\mosquitto.exe" -v

Purpose:
Runs the MQTT broker and receives sensor data from ESP32 devices.

Port:
1883

Keep this terminal running.

---

## Terminal 2 — AI Service

Run:

cd D:\Lifeguard_ai\backend
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe ai_service.py

Purpose:
Runs the Random Forest AI model and SHAP explainability service.

Port:
8000

Expected output:

Successfully loaded Random Forest Model and SHAP Explainer.

Keep this terminal running.

---

## Terminal 3 — Node.js Backend

Run:

cd D:\Lifeguard_ai\backend
node server.js

Purpose:
Handles MQTT data, patient baseline calculation, AI communication, MongoDB storage and alerts.

Port:
5000

Expected output should include:

MongoDB connected
Server running on port 5000
MQTT connected

Keep this terminal running.

---

## Terminal 4 — Testing / IoT

Run:

cd D:\Lifeguard_ai\backend

This terminal is used for testing and later for ESP32 integration.

### Reset Patient Baseline

Current patient:

Patient ID: P001
Room: R101

Run:

Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:5000/api/patients/P001/baseline/reset" -Method POST

### Run Baseline Demo

node demo/baseline-demo.js

This sends 10 normal readings and establishes the patient's personalized baseline.

### Run Abnormal Demo

node demo/abnormal-demo.js

### Check Patient Result

Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:5000/api/patients/P001"

---

# IoT Team — Continue From Here

The current software uses simulated MQTT data.

The next task is to replace:

demo/baseline-demo.js
demo/abnormal-demo.js

with the actual ESP32 patient monitoring node.

## Patient MQTT Topic

Publish patient vitals to:

lifeguard/patient/P001/vitals

## Required JSON Format

{
    "heartRate": 78,
    "spo2": 97,
    "temperature": 36.8
}

Required field names:

heartRate
spo2
temperature

Do not change these field names or the MQTT topic structure without coordinating with the software team.

